22.  * `DateTimeInput` happens to emit today (a trailing `Z`) — the row's own
23.  * type (`TimeOfDeathRow`'s doc comment) already documents that an offset
24.  * form is equally valid on the wire. An empty string is rejected: `""` is
25.  * this type's own "unanswered" marker (`isEmptyRow`, below), and a row that
26.  * reaches the edit log via the assistant is asserting an actual death time,
27.  * not a deliberately blank one — clearing the section is `single.clearRow()`
28.  * (an `op: "remove"`), never an `add`/`update` with a blank patch.
